- **Noisy commands** (tests, builds, `git log`/`diff`, searches, listings): prefer `repowise distill <cmd>`, the same command with its exit code preserved and errors-first output. A `[repowise#<ref>: N lines omitted]` marker is recoverable via `repowise expand <ref>` (add `-q <regex>` to filter); never re-run the command to see omitted output.
- **Settings** (options, cost, turning something off): `repowise config list` (`--area <area>` or `--changed`) and `repowise config explain <key>`; ask the user before `repowise config set <key> <value>`.
{% if data.record_decisions %}
- **Recording a decision** you had to reason out: `repowise decision add --agent <your slug> --decision D --rationale '<why, what you rejected>' --affects <path> --evidence-commit <sha>` records it without prompting and prints the id (`--format json` to parse it back); the slug names you, e.g. `claude_code`. It comes into force when that commit merges to the default branch. Records mined from history are background: `get_why` serves them when asked. To put one in force yourself, `repowise decision confirm <id> --agent <your slug>` (add `--reason`, `--scope`, `--evidence` or `--decision` for a missing part); `dismiss`, `merge` and `deprecate` take `--agent` too. These are signed as yours; a repository with agent acceptance off refuses them.
{% endif %}
